From b0509d39d81d00e61048e4698460ddd4955cab00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 14:43:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Prose Display (S2): virtio shared memory + prose_display
 driver

virtio bus manager / virtio_pci: parse VIRTIO_PCI_CAP_SHARED_MEMORY_CFG
(cap type 8, 64-bit offset/length, BAR relative) and expose the regions
through a new get_shared_memory() entry at the end of both the controller
and the device interfaces (positional tables: appended, nothing shifts).

prose_display: kernel driver for the Prose Display device (virtio ID 63,
docs/s2-display-device.md in HaikuArmQemu). Negotiates VSYNC|RESIZE,
reads the 64-byte config, maps shared memory region 0 (the surface pool)
write-back, allocates controlq/eventq, posts 8 event buffers, enables
events, sets the preferred mode and publishes graphics/prose_display/0
(ioctls for the coming accelerant: GET_SHARED_INFO, SET_MODE, COMMIT,
ENABLE_EVENTS). Milestone A: it draws a colour-bar test pattern and
animates a box with two-rect commits from a kernel thread (PRDS_TEST_PATTERN),
so the whole pipe is verified with no accelerant yet.

Verified on Virtualization.framework (hvgpu --display s2): region 0
appears as BAR 4 at 0x180000000, mode 1280x800 stride 5120, ~10
commits/s, host snapshot shows the pattern.

arm64 note: an area cannot be kernel-RW/user-RO (arch_vm_supports_protection),
so the shared info area is kernel-only + B_CLONEABLE_AREA.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
